00:10:57,421 --> 00:10:59,900
or at least not yet.

220
00:10:59,901 --> 00:11:02,360
When you think about barbecue or burgers,

221
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:07,740
grilling in the backyard, we love to feed the beast.

222
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:11,820
The commercial ability of basically making you be able

223
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:13,940
to have meat at any moment that you want to

224
00:11:14,020 --> 00:11:16,880
by going to a supermarket has made it so that we feel

225
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:20,020
that it's simple, that it's a natural part of our diet.

226
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:22,260
You won't be disappointed in these takes, man.

227
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:25,300
That Norman Rockwell image of the table of plenty

228
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:28,520
with the big turkey is so incredibly

229
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:30,520
20th century American dream.

