00:21:07,841 --> 00:21:11,840
To this day, the military is researching technological advances

432
00:21:11,841 --> 00:21:14,840
that could bring us our future favorite foods.

433
00:21:14,841 --> 00:21:15,840
This is Dr. Ann Barrett.

434
00:21:15,841 --> 00:21:16,840
Hi, Doc.

435
00:21:16,841 --> 00:21:19,840
Ann is an expert in a novel compression technology

436
00:21:19,841 --> 00:21:22,840
called ultrasonic agglomeration.

437
00:21:22,841 --> 00:21:25,000
Ultrasonic agglomeration was first developed

438
00:21:25,001 --> 00:21:27,720
for the plastics industry, but it was Dr. Anne

439
00:21:27,721 --> 00:21:31,480
and her colleagues who adapted that high technology to food.

440
00:21:31,481 --> 00:21:34,920
It uses ultrasonic vibrations and energy

441
00:21:34,921 --> 00:21:39,960
to almost melt powdered foods and transform it into a solid.

442
00:21:39,961 --> 00:21:43,760
We are taking the tropical fruit powders,

443
00:21:43,761 --> 00:21:47,000
which actually contain real fruits and vegetables.

444
00:21:47,001 --> 00:21:48,300
OK.

445
00:21:48,301 --> 00:21:49,800
And we're going to weld them into a small,

446
00:21:49,801 --> 00:21:51,800
chewable candy type of product.

447
00:21:51,801 --> 00:21:53,140
All right, I'm gonna watch this happen.

448
00:21:53,141 --> 00:21:54,140
All right.

449
00:21:54,141 --> 00:21:55,440
This is an ultrasonic horn.

450
00:21:55,441 --> 00:21:56,440
Uh-huh.

451
00:21:56,441 --> 00:21:59,040
It's vibrating ultrasonically, so it will make sound.

452
00:21:59,041 --> 00:22:01,040
The sound waves cause vibrations

453
00:22:01,041 --> 00:22:02,640
on the powdered fruit particles,

454
00:22:02,641 --> 00:22:05,740
so they rub against each other at a very fast rate.

455
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:08,720
That causes friction, which also causes heat,

456
00:22:08,721 --> 00:22:11,520
making the surfaces melt or soften.

457
00:22:11,521 --> 00:22:14,520
Then the compression component of the machine

458
00:22:14,521 --> 00:22:16,560
forces the heated particles together,

459
00:22:16,561 --> 00:22:20,520
so the softened surfaces can melt together and form a solid.

460
00:22:20,521 --> 00:22:24,320
Dr. Anne places about 15 grams of dried powdered fruit

461
00:22:24,321 --> 00:22:26,000
under the ultrasonic horn.

462
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:30,560
I heard it.

463
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:31,700
I felt it in my teeth.

464
00:22:32,260 --> 00:22:32,960
Wow.

465
00:22:33,440 --> 00:22:34,400
See how fast that is?

466
00:22:34,740 --> 00:22:37,000
The powdered fruit is now compressed

467
00:22:37,001 --> 00:22:39,940
into a chewy, vitamin-packed candy snack,

468
00:22:40,260 --> 00:22:42,840
giving soldiers the vitamin boost they need.

