00:23:08,380 --> 00:23:10,880
So far, so good.

479
00:23:10,980 --> 00:23:12,880
There's a faint kind of carrot-y note.

480
00:23:12,980 --> 00:23:14,380
There's carrot in it.

481
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:15,280
Yeah.

482
00:23:15,380 --> 00:23:16,280
This is crazy.

483
00:23:16,380 --> 00:23:17,620
This was powder.

484
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:20,020
And I've already identified different real fruits.

485
00:23:20,021 --> 00:23:21,360
fruits that are in it.

486
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:30,300
Powder manifesting into food has changed the future of food

487
00:23:30,301 --> 00:23:31,640
before.

488
00:23:31,641 --> 00:23:35,200
It's beater-licking delicious and as easy as pie,

489
00:23:35,201 --> 00:23:37,900
except it's cake in a box.

490
00:23:37,901 --> 00:23:40,500
Guaranteed perfect every time you bake.

491
00:23:40,501 --> 00:23:42,180
Cake after cake after cake.

492
00:23:42,181 --> 00:23:45,480
Boxed cake mix is so common to us today.

493
00:23:45,481 --> 00:23:48,480
But before the 1930s, if you wanted a cake,

494
00:23:48,481 --> 00:23:51,560
you had to make it entirely from scratch.

495
00:23:51,561 --> 00:23:56,340
The box of dried cake mix was officially patented in 1933

496
00:23:56,341 --> 00:23:58,880
by John D. Duff from Pennsylvania.

497
00:23:58,881 --> 00:24:01,920
His molasses company had a supply surplus.

498
00:24:01,921 --> 00:24:03,720
So rather than toss it out,

499
00:24:03,721 --> 00:24:08,000
Duff figured out how to successfully dehydrate molasses

500
00:24:08,001 --> 00:24:11,720
into powder, which he mixed with other powdered ingredients

501
00:24:11,721 --> 00:24:15,340
to make cake, like flour, sugar, salt, and baking soda.

502
00:24:15,341 --> 00:24:18,080
His original use was for gingerbread cake

503
00:24:18,081 --> 00:24:21,680
And in a subsequent patent, he also introduced mixes

504
00:24:21,681 --> 00:24:24,920
for white, spice, and devil's food cake.

505
00:24:24,921 --> 00:24:27,220
But it wasn't until post-World War II

506
00:24:27,221 --> 00:24:30,960
that we learned to love the convenience of just adding eggs.

507
00:24:30,961 --> 00:24:34,320
This act of cracking fresh eggs and mixing them

508
00:24:34,321 --> 00:24:36,560
into a conveniently prepared cake mix,

509
00:24:36,561 --> 00:24:38,600
like Duncan Hines or Betty Crocker,

510
00:24:38,601 --> 00:24:42,740
made us feel like we actually baked a cake from scratch

511
00:24:42,741 --> 00:24:46,140
without actually having to bake a cake from scratch.

512
00:24:46,141 --> 00:24:50,400
A light and tender Betty Crocker yellow cake.

513
00:24:50,401 --> 00:24:51,180
Perfect.

514
00:24:51,181 --> 00:24:52,140
Anytime.

515
00:24:52,141 --> 00:24:55,800
The indispensable convenience of powdered cake mix

516
00:24:55,801 --> 00:24:58,020
revolutionized baking.

517
00:24:58,021 --> 00:25:00,540
It meant that any meal could be as special as a birthday

518
00:25:00,541 --> 00:25:03,920
celebration by just adding eggs.

519
00:25:03,921 --> 00:25:07,680
Dehydrated cake mix isn't the only dried food

520
00:25:07,681 --> 00:25:09,880
that revolutionized the food industry.

521
00:25:09,881 --> 00:25:14,020
The military has been dehydrating foods since World War II,

522
00:25:14,021 --> 00:25:16,480
using what was then a cutting-edge technique,

523
00:25:16,481 --> 00:25:17,920
the freeze-dry method.

524
00:25:17,921 --> 00:25:21,840
And that new technique bled into now-famous favorites

